  m_Name: SpaceStation
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  exhibitName: Space Station
  description: "A space station is a large structure that orbits Earth and serves
    as a home and workplace for astronauts. It is designed for long-term missions
    in space, where scientists and engineers can perform experiments that cannot
    be done on Earth. Space stations have living areas, laboratories, and equipment
    to keep astronauts safe and healthy in zero gravity. \n\nThe most famous space
    station today is the International Space Station (ISS), which is a joint project
    by several countries, including the United States, Russia, Japan, Canada, and
    European nations. Astronauts on the ISS study things like how plants grow in
    space, how the human body changes without gravity, and how to build better technology
    for future space travel. Space stations are important because they help us learn
    more about space and prepare for missions to the Moon and Mars. "
  images: []
